Time Complexity:

Let n = size of array

    Each index is pushed once and popped once → O(n)

Overall: O(n)


Space Complexity:

    Stack stores indices → O(n)
    Result list → O(n)

Overall: O(n)


Approach:

1. Create a stack to store indices of days
   - Stack maintains decreasing stock prices

2. Traverse array from left to right:

   - While stack is not empty and current price ≥ price at stack top:
     → pop indices (they are not useful anymore)

3. After popping:
   - If stack is empty → span = i + 1
   - Else → span = i - st.peek()

4. Add span to result list

5. Push current index into stack

6. Continue for all elements

7. Return the result list




class Solution {
    public ArrayList<Integer> calculateSpan(int[] arr) {
        ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();
        Stack<Integer> st = new Stack<>();
        for(int i=0; i<arr.length; i++){
            while(st.size()>0 && arr[i]>=arr[st.peek()]) st.pop();
            
            if(st.size()==0) list.add(i+1);
            else list.add(i-st.peek());
            
            st.push(i);
        }
        return list;
    }
}
